  "citations": [
    {
      "ref": "TMA1995/s43",
      "quote": "An application for the registration of a trade mark in respect of particular goods or services must be rejected if, because of some connotation that the trade mark or a sign contained in the trade mark has, the use of the trade mark in relation to those goods or services would be likely to deceive or cause confusion."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part32A/2/4/2/4/1",
      "quote": "If a trade mark contains or consists of material that connotes a particular plant variety, it would be deceptive or confusing if the trade mark was applied to goods which are a different variety of the same or closely related genus."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part32A/2/4/2/4/1",
      "quote": "In such a circumstance, a ground for rejection under section 43 is applicable."
    },
    {
      "ref": "TMM/Part32A/2/4/2/4/1",
      "quote": "Therefore, if the trade mark contains or consists of a known variety name, the connotation may be immediate, and deception or confusion is likely if the trade mark is used on a different variety of the same or a closely related genus. However, the examiner needs to consider how the variety name appears within the trade mark as a whole. For example, if the plant name is a dictionary word appearing in a phrase then connotation may not be immediate."
    }
  ],
  "answer": "Yes, in principle—but the key concern is use on a DIFFERENT variety of the same or a closely related genus, not merely that the plants share a genus.\n\nAct: Section 43 requires rejection where a connotation of the trade mark, or a sign within it, makes use on the claimed goods likely to deceive or cause confusion [TMA1995/s43].\n\nManual practice: The Manual identifies a section 43 ground where a mark connotes a particular plant variety but is applied to a different variety of the same or a closely related genus [TMM/Part32A/2/4/2/4/1]. However, the examiner must consider the mark as a whole and whether the variety connotation is immediate. A variety name that is also a dictionary word within a phrase may not convey that immediate connotation [TMM/Part32A/2/4/2/4/1]. This is general examination guidance, not a determination of your application's outcome."
}
